01:45.660 --> 01:49.620
Yokohama - International Stadium

01:50.760 --> 01:55.350
It's time for the Japanese international challenge.  It's Japan versus the Netherlands.

01:55.350 --> 01:58.140
It's almost time for kick-off.

01:58.140 --> 02:03.530
This game against the Dutch should prove to be an important game in gauging

02:03.530 --> 02:05.930
the Japanese team's ability for winning the International Cup.

02:06.390 --> 02:11.400
It's a highly anticipated game in all of Japan... No, the world has been waiting for this game.

02:19.850 --> 02:23.790
Introducing the players of both teams.

02:24.420 --> 02:28.430
Dutch player Number 1, Var Len Fort.

02:30.660 --> 02:33.530
Number 8, Willem Arminius.

02:34.830 --> 02:37.950
Number 14, Albert Potter.

02:39.400 --> 02:41.720
Number 9, Bernhardt Tasman.

02:41.720 --> 02:45.960
Tsubasa-chan and his team are playing in such a nice stadium. They really are stars!

02:45.960 --> 02:49.420
Yes. My husband is really looking forward to today's game, too.

02:49.420 --> 02:52.310
International games really are impressive!

02:52.310 --> 02:54.420
I'm so excited!

02:55.070 --> 02:58.720
Next, introducing the Japanese team.

02:59.120 --> 03:02.120
Number 1, Wakabayashi Genzo.

03:05.030 --> 03:07.370
Number 4, Ishizaki Ryo.

03:09.280 --> 03:11.610
Number 7, Soda Makoto.

03:13.090 --> 03:15.330
Number 5, Jito Hiroshi.

03:17.210 --> 03:19.810
Number 12, Matsuyama Hikaru.

03:21.310 --> 03:23.780
Number 11, Misaki Taro.

03:25.150 --> 03:27.700
Number 10, Ohzora Tsubasa.

03:29.180 --> 03:31.730
Number 15, Sawada Takeshi.

03:33.150 --> 03:35.790
Number 13, Taki Hajime.

03:37.200 --> 03:39.680
Number 18, Nitta Shun.

03:41.230 --> 03:43.460
Number 9, Hyuga Kojiro.

03:43.460 --> 03:45.360
Look, it's your brother!

03:45.360 --> 03:47.260
You're so awesome, brother!

03:47.700 --> 03:50.780
These are the players for the Japanese team.

03:47.810 --> 03:50.780
Good luck, Tsubasa!

03:51.280 --> 03:53.600
The Dutch team has assembled their best players,

03:53.600 --> 03:58.080
{nihon wa}while the Japanese team is made up of the Junior Youth Tournament roster,

03:58.080 --> 04:00.780
{daihyou chiimu}when they won the championship four years ago.

04:00.780 --> 04:04.520
Japan is making its first challenge toward the International Cup,

04:04.870 --> 04:07.450
and this game is our first big step!

04:12.900 --> 04:18.010
<b>Newly-Born Japanese Team</b>

04:12.900 --> 04:18.010
<b>Newly-Born Japanese Team</b>

04:30.260 --> 04:33.730
They're all huge!

04:34.530 --> 04:38.250
That Gustaf guy's a monster!

04:52.030 --> 04:55.580
Hyuga. I'll run circles around you today.

04:56.130 --> 05:00.580
Let's see you try. I'll settle the score today!

05:08.570 --> 05:10.220
Let's have a good game.

05:10.220 --> 05:14.590
This game is a good opportunity for us to redeem ourselves to the world,

05:14.590 --> 05:17.060
{sekai ni}now that we failed to qualify for the International Cup.

05:17.060 --> 05:18.040
Tsubasa.

05:18.040 --> 05:19.980
We're not going to hold anything back.

05:20.850 --> 05:22.220
I expect nothing less.

05:22.220 --> 05:25.220
But we won't be easily defeated.

05:27.590 --> 05:32.540
They are players with high-level individual skills who work as a team to attack and defend.

05:32.540 --> 05:35.410
That's Dutch ultra-offensive Total Football.

05:35.410 --> 05:37.220
This is going to be a tough game.

05:38.230 --> 05:42.890
Just how far the Japanese team desires to advance in the International Cup

05:42.890 --> 05:47.780
{sekai no}will become clear in this game against the Dutch, a leading team in the world.

05:47.780 --> 05:50.260
Katagiri has chosen a great opponent for us.

05:51.360 --> 05:53.970
Players of both teams are in their positions.

05:53.970 --> 05:55.820
The game will begin shortly.

05:57.110 --> 06:01.160
Katagiri. Our Dutch players will not hold anything back.

06:01.160 --> 06:05.510
Let's see how well your team full of young players can keep up with us.

06:06.300 --> 06:14.130
Japan! Japan! Japan!

06:11.280 --> 06:14.140
The stage for our international challenge has been set.

06:14.140 --> 06:17.480
Show the world what the future of Japanese soccer is all about.

06:18.110 --> 06:19.300
I'm counting on you all.

06:20.560 --> 06:26.300
Coach Edward, did you come all the way to Japan to see Ohzora Tsubasa play?

06:26.300 --> 06:30.060
The game between my fatherland, the Netherlands,

06:30.060 --> 06:34.240
and the International Cup host, Japan, is of great interest to me.

06:34.240 --> 06:36.320
I do not have any other motives.

06:44.820 --> 06:50.830
Japan may have Tsubasa, but they won't stand a chance against the Dutch, Roberto.

06:50.830 --> 06:54.340
No. Even I can't tell how this game will play out.

07:07.380 --> 07:09.220
Japan kicks off.

07:11.700 --> 07:13.580
We're playing against the Dutch.

07:13.580 --> 07:17.080
Let's make the first move before they get into the groove!

07:17.530 --> 07:20.820
Ohzora Tsubasa rushes forward immediately after kick-off.

07:20.820 --> 07:22.610
Misaki follows!

07:23.570 --> 07:26.240
Tsubasa, draw as many as you can.

07:26.240 --> 07:27.540
Free me up for a pass!

07:29.260 --> 07:31.420
Japan is really charged up, huh?

07:33.300 --> 07:35.140
Ohzora passes to Misaki!

07:35.140 --> 07:37.740
They are charging into their opponent's territory with well-coordinated passes.

07:39.130 --> 07:40.820
Ohzora advances!

07:41.970 --> 07:43.370
Hyuga is in front of him.

07:43.370 --> 07:45.160
They're running toward the goal!

07:45.820 --> 07:48.540
Tsubasa! Pass me the ball!

07:48.540 --> 07:49.580
Got it!

07:50.170 --> 07:52.620
Japan attacks early in the game!

08:01.100 --> 08:01.780
Hyuga-kun!

08:02.540 --> 08:04.300
Could this be a chance for Japan to take the first goal?

08:06.490 --> 08:08.020
Take this, Netherlands!

08:08.860 --> 08:11.380
The largest Dutch defender, Gustaf, stands in his way!

08:11.380 --> 08:12.740
You're in the way! Get out!

08:12.740 --> 08:14.260
Hyuga shoots!

08:19.340 --> 08:21.740
The Tiger Shot strikes Gustaf!

08:21.740 --> 08:22.660
What?!

08:23.100 --> 08:26.200
Gustaf stopped Hyuga's shot with his body.

08:26.200 --> 08:27.530
It didn't even phase him!

08:27.530 --> 08:28.950
He is truly the "Wall of Steel."

08:28.950 --> 08:30.660
The "Human Mountain!"

08:33.390 --> 08:35.180
Don't give up yet, Japan.

08:38.130 --> 08:41.420
Someone of his size must have slow horizontal movements.

08:45.610 --> 08:48.160
Gustaf blew Misaki away!

08:49.100 --> 08:49.780
Misaki-kun!

08:51.890 --> 08:54.050
Gustaf sends the ball to their front line with a long kick.

08:54.050 --> 08:56.140
Japan has failed to capitalize on their chance!

08:56.140 --> 08:58.140
All of the Dutch players are moving forward!

08:58.140 --> 09:00.340
Their attack begins!

09:03.630 --> 09:07.180
That was your first and the last chance, Japan!

09:07.800 --> 09:10.000
Willem dribbles forward for the attack!

09:10.000 --> 09:11.160
He's fast!

09:12.260 --> 09:13.780
Are you ready for this?

09:13.780 --> 09:16.780
He's coming! Keep the defensive line intact!

09:17.440 --> 09:18.780
A-All right!

09:35.740 --> 09:37.740
I won't let you get free!

09:39.320 --> 09:40.740
Fight on, Japan.

09:45.560 --> 09:46.660
Damn it.

09:46.660 --> 09:48.950
Willem is already in front of the goal!

09:51.940 --> 09:53.660
I'll stop you!

09:53.660 --> 09:56.500
He's just going to charge forward like an idiot?

09:56.500 --> 09:57.660
Watch and learn!

09:57.660 --> 09:59.000
Is he shooting?

09:59.500 --> 10:00.840
It's a pass!

10:01.260 --> 10:04.260
Albert is running forward like a bullet!

10:04.670 --> 10:05.980
Sawada can't keep up!

10:06.770 --> 10:07.980
He's one-on-one with the goalkeeper!

10:07.980 --> 10:10.500
We got the first goal!

10:10.940 --> 10:12.950
I won't let you score so easily!

10:24.610 --> 10:26.660
Wakabayashi stopped it!

10:27.290 --> 10:29.480
Limiting his shoot course was a good decision.

10:29.480 --> 10:32.680
He used a diving catch to stop the ball from point-blank range

10:32.680 --> 10:34.760
and defended Japan's goal.

10:34.760 --> 10:36.700
He truly is Japan's Godly Protector!

10:43.290 --> 10:45.380
The ball is heading toward Ohzora in the midfield!

10:47.980 --> 10:49.740
Good work, Wakabayashi-kun!

10:50.450 --> 10:51.580
Okay. Let's go!

10:51.580 --> 10:53.180
Watch out, Tsubasa-kun!

10:56.930 --> 10:59.940
Like I said, you don't have any more chances!

11:00.900 --> 11:02.940
He's fast! A lot faster than I imagined!

11:03.930 --> 11:06.990
Ohzora was crushed by Willem's tackle!

11:06.990 --> 11:10.460
His athletic skills are Willem's key advantage in this game.

11:10.460 --> 11:13.460
Taki! Don't give him space! Stop him in the midfield!

11:13.460 --> 11:15.300
I'll stop him no matter what!

11:15.300 --> 11:17.300
I won't let you do as you please!

11:17.770 --> 11:19.850
The Japanese team is surrounding him!

11:35.380 --> 11:37.820
It's a powerful surprise shot!

11:42.060 --> 11:43.980
Wakabayashi knocked it away!

11:43.980 --> 11:45.500
And there's Bernhardt running toward the loose ball!

11:50.620 --> 11:53.140
Goal!

11:53.590 --> 11:56.140
Netherlands scores the first goal!

11:56.610 --> 11:59.750
It hasn't been ten minutes since the game started.

11:59.750 --> 12:04.530
The Japanese team already allowed a goal to the merciless attack of the Dutchmen!

12:07.650 --> 12:12.160
Is Japan powerless against the Dutch Total Football?

12:13.740 --> 12:16.140
Good luck, Japan.

12:30.590 --> 12:34.920
The Japanese team has allowed the Netherlands to take the lead just ten minutes into the first half.

12:34.920 --> 12:37.740
The game resumes as they try to catch up.

12:38.800 --> 12:40.350
Look at this!

12:40.350 --> 12:42.850
They've pushed their two side defenders to the front line.

12:42.850 --> 12:45.860
It's the original Dutch 2-4-4 offensive formation.

12:45.860 --> 12:48.510
Are they trying to increase their lead?

12:48.510 --> 12:49.760
Katagiri-kun.

12:49.760 --> 12:55.020
Maybe the Dutch are too strong for a team consisting solely of young players.

12:55.520 --> 13:03.020
Y-Yeah! If Japan loses big, the JFA might be blamed for taking a foolish strategy!

13:03.020 --> 13:05.590
{masukomi}The press is going to have a field day with this!

13:05.590 --> 13:06.900
We're doomed!

13:06.900 --> 13:09.350
I'm betting our future on them.

13:09.350 --> 13:15.780
If they lose big, then I am prepared to accept all responsibility for this.

13:18.210 --> 13:22.100
However, the game has only begun.

13:31.020 --> 13:34.450
He couldn't break through the Dutch defensive line!

13:34.450 --> 13:36.820
This is a trial that we must pass through.

13:37.340 --> 13:44.550
The new generation must open the path for Japan to clear the hurdle of international soccer.

13:44.550 --> 13:48.100
{sore niwa}They are best suited for this role.

13:52.700 --> 13:54.730
Japan is completely at the mercy of the Dutch.

13:54.730 --> 13:58.700
Their all-in attack approaches the Japanese goal like a tsunami!

14:16.840 --> 14:17.940
I got this!

14:21.500 --> 14:22.740
Bernhardt shoots!

14:26.660 --> 14:28.580
Is it a goal?

14:29.750 --> 14:31.620
Oh, Ohzora's there!

14:33.340 --> 14:38.130
Ohzora got all the way back and defended the Japanese goal with his body!

14:41.870 --> 14:43.640
You saved me there, Tsubasa.

14:47.720 --> 14:48.810
No problem.

14:48.810 --> 14:50.320
The Dutch team is impressive.

14:50.320 --> 14:51.470
They're so fast and strong.

14:51.470 --> 14:52.340
Yeah.

14:54.940 --> 14:57.380
It's a throw-in for the Netherlands.

15:04.620 --> 15:05.540
Damn you!

15:17.810 --> 15:19.420
I won't let you score again!

15:28.780 --> 15:29.380
Hyuga!

15:34.350 --> 15:35.260
You punk!

15:36.730 --> 15:38.870
I thought you were going to settle the scores today.

15:38.870 --> 15:40.260
Bring it on.

15:40.630 --> 15:41.780
Good!

15:42.770 --> 15:45.800
Hyuga and Willem battle for the ball in midfield!

15:49.730 --> 15:51.820
Hyuga manages to keep the ball!

15:53.820 --> 15:56.100
You've still got much to learn, Hyuga!

15:56.100 --> 15:57.740
You'll pay for this!

15:57.740 --> 16:00.340
Willem forcefully took the ball!

16:00.340 --> 16:02.650
The Piemonte teammates go at it!

16:03.700 --> 16:06.480
Japan has failed to reach the Dutch goal.

16:12.140 --> 16:14.140
Don't let them get open with the ball!

16:14.140 --> 16:16.140
Ishizaki! Soda! Jito!

16:16.590 --> 16:18.060
I-I know!

16:26.310 --> 16:27.340
I won't let it pass through!

16:28.260 --> 16:30.170
Ohzora cuts off the pass!

16:30.170 --> 16:32.320
He stopped their chance!

16:32.320 --> 16:33.540
Tsubasa.

16:33.540 --> 16:36.740
Japan is hopeless if you have to defend.

16:36.740 --> 16:38.260
I won't let it end like this!

16:38.750 --> 16:41.090
Ohzora is surrounded by Dutch players.

16:41.090 --> 16:42.780
He can't get the ball out!

16:42.780 --> 16:44.580
Don't lose! Tsubasa!

16:44.580 --> 16:46.060
Go, Japan!

16:46.990 --> 16:49.690
It's almost 35 minutes into the first half.

16:49.690 --> 16:51.160
There are only ten minutes remaining.

16:51.160 --> 16:56.840
It's not just Ohzora. Everyone but Hyuga is defending for Japan.

16:56.840 --> 17:00.580
They are preventing the Dutch from scoring again, but they can't attack!

17:00.580 --> 17:04.580
Pass me the ball somehow!

17:06.730 --> 17:08.380
Albert got the ball out!

17:08.380 --> 17:09.900
The ball is back to Willem!

17:10.360 --> 17:13.380
He glides through the field like a jet fighter!

17:18.560 --> 17:19.220
Willem!

17:23.830 --> 17:25.460
It's Ohzora!

17:25.460 --> 17:27.980
Ohzora Tsubasa clears the ball again!

17:31.270 --> 17:33.500
The Dutch are attacking with all their players.

17:33.500 --> 17:35.600
Even if we stop their forwards, it's no use.

17:35.600 --> 17:40.580
They're all highly skilled, well-rounded players.

17:41.000 --> 17:42.300
Damn it.

17:42.300 --> 17:46.300
We're not doing our jobs if Tsubasa has to defend the whole time.

17:47.600 --> 17:50.470
It's still the first half, but...

17:52.450 --> 17:55.300
Damn it! The Dutch are good!

17:55.300 --> 17:59.870
It looks like the Japanese team is stuck in front of the goal.

17:59.870 --> 18:00.750
Yeah.

18:00.750 --> 18:04.300
Even Tsubasa is defending, and they're barely holding them off.

18:04.300 --> 18:07.870
Somehow, they have to create an opportunity, so they can attack.

18:08.300 --> 18:09.620
It's the Dutch team's throw-in.

18:20.780 --> 18:22.020
I won't let you score again!

18:23.630 --> 18:25.020
What a fine save by Wakabayashi!

18:25.020 --> 18:26.310
He protected the goal!

18:26.310 --> 18:28.020
He managed to protect the goal!

18:28.890 --> 18:31.060
Less than five minutes are remaining in the first half.

18:31.750 --> 18:34.780
Go, Tsubasa!

18:31.950 --> 18:34.780
{STACK}Japan can't let the Dutch score again!

18:35.470 --> 18:38.890
The Dutch will attack, without rest, to the end, Katagiri.

18:39.340 --> 18:43.550
If Japan suffers an embarrassing defeat in this game,

18:43.550 --> 18:49.890
it would mean your soccer is still child's play at the world-class level.

18:50.780 --> 18:54.790
Ah! This game is bad for my heart.

18:54.790 --> 18:59.820
Coach! I can't stand to sit and watch japan go through this crisis!

19:00.470 --> 19:03.660
I won't change any players during the first 45 minutes.

19:03.660 --> 19:07.130
Aoi, I feel the same way.

19:07.660 --> 19:14.420
That's exactly why we have to observe the Dutch players' movement and memorize everything.

19:14.960 --> 19:19.470
That's our job now, so Japan can make a comeback in the second half.

19:21.700 --> 19:23.060
Misugi-san...

19:27.490 --> 19:30.950
There must be an opportunity for a comeback.

19:32.360 --> 19:34.950
Hang in there, Japan!

19:34.950 --> 19:39.190
They only allowed one goal after getting pressed by the Dutch the whole game.

19:39.190 --> 19:41.060
Japan is doing pretty well.

19:41.570 --> 19:44.150
Hang in there, Tsubasa!

19:44.150 --> 19:47.060
The world awaits you beyond this wall!

19:49.480 --> 19:52.060
Ohzora dribbles ahead with the ball!

19:52.680 --> 19:54.330
That's it, Tsubasa!

19:54.330 --> 19:55.970
{aite}It doesn't matter if you're playing against the Dutch.

19:55.970 --> 19:58.200
{ball wo}Just head toward the goal whenever you have the ball!

19:58.200 --> 20:00.320
That's your soccer!

20:00.320 --> 20:02.580
There's not much time left in the first half!

20:02.580 --> 20:04.300
This is as far as you'll get!

20:07.290 --> 20:08.700
Willem goes for a sliding tackle!

20:09.270 --> 20:11.660
Ohzora is off balance!

20:12.760 --> 20:13.780
Hyuga-kun!

20:14.540 --> 20:16.620
Ohzora launches an off-balance pass!

20:17.150 --> 20:18.860
The ball reaches Hyuga,

20:18.860 --> 20:21.230
but the Gustaf the Giant stands in his way!

20:21.230 --> 20:22.580
He showed up again.

20:23.040 --> 20:24.630
I've got to get past him.

20:24.630 --> 20:26.100
I can't see the goal!

20:26.870 --> 20:29.300
There's only the stoppage time in this half!

20:29.300 --> 20:31.380
If the Tiger Shot doesn't work,

20:31.380 --> 20:33.380
then how about this?!

20:33.890 --> 20:35.680
Hyuga prepares to shoot!

20:42.100 --> 20:42.820
A lob shot!

20:43.300 --> 20:45.700
He took Gustaf off guard with a lob shot!

20:45.700 --> 20:47.220
It's heading towards the goal!

20:48.580 --> 20:51.100
Folt stopped it!

20:52.120 --> 20:57.370
Folt, the goalkeeper, reacted well to Hyuga's surprise shot.

20:57.370 --> 20:59.820
The Dutch wall is not easy to break.

21:01.300 --> 21:03.830
That's the end of the first half.

21:03.830 --> 21:07.140
Japan could not tie the game.

21:12.990 --> 21:15.540
Even after dodging Willem and getting past Gustaf,

21:15.540 --> 21:18.860
the Dutch still have Folt, the prominent goalkeeper.

21:18.860 --> 21:22.860
Is it impossible for Japan to score a goal against the Dutch?

21:22.860 --> 21:26.310
He got past Gustaf's height with a lob shot.

21:26.310 --> 21:31.860
It was on target, but you're not going to get a goal from me with a shot like that.

